00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
warhammer 40 000 road trader is the  first game of its kind to exist in the  40k universe but what does it mean for  rogue trader and for warhammer games as  a whole i caught up with alexander gusev  the creative director for road trader at  owlcat games to find out a little more  about warhammer 40k's first crpg what  it's offering to warhammer fans the  game's characters the setting of rogue  trader and more one of the key things is  that in the world of 40k rogue trader  dynasties have an incredible amount of  freedom due to their warrant of trade  this is a letter of appointment that  elevates their authority to that that  may sometimes equal space marines and  even planetary governors some were even  signed by the emperor himself this  incredible freedom within the 40k  universe can now translate to the  freedom of the player you can go to  places where other people really go  you're also given more freedom than  almost anyone within the setting you're  also given more freedom and how you  interact with others like for example  most imperial servants will  only be able to interact with zenith in  the way of killing them while you can  actually talk to them and it is  not completely heresy alexander alluded  to some of the potential party members  that may be available to you in your  travels and only accessible due to your  freedom and status while i was told most  of your party would be human in nature  some are  less human than others there are  individuals such as a space marine a  sister of battle and navigator of the  war a selection of psyches both  sanctioned and unsanctioned but when it  comes to fully non-human xenos party  members concerning non-human races there  are elderly ranger featured on the gear  and that's not not the only zenith  companion you will have now what those  races could be we may have to wait a  little while to find out perhaps a crew  mercenary maybe a squat to tie in with  games workshop's release of leagues of  voltan or maybe even a jokero companion  i'm looking forward to reading your  theories in the comment section below  but who are these characters going to be  who are you going to be i asked about  things like classes and careers and how  your rogue trade will start and grow  through your campaign alex said that  they have a career system that will  reflect both the background of your  character but also the abilities  available to you as you level up through  the game in the lore of warhammer many  rogue traders start off as members of  the imperial guard navy merchants  planetary commanders or even in rare  cases part of the inquisition with these  concept artworks that alka shared with  me we know of at least two potential  backgrounds a commissar and a crime lord  with no doubt many more to come how this  connects to your ancestor theodora the  individual we saw in the trailer we  don't yet know only that you are her  heir but potentially not the most direct  descendant or even first choice to take  up the mantle of rogue trader it appears  then that this rogue-traded dynasty was  created and has thrived way before your  character's status was elevated and  therefore there's both a ship under your  command and worlds under your influence  your ship is a giant cathedral fortress  factory so there will be some adventures  within the ship itself about the dynasty  the most important part the dynasty  gives you is the third trade empire  within corona expense it has some walls  within it one of them for example is  janus it's a world covered in jungle  that was uh repurposed because of its  plant life it was reversed proposed for  agriculture and uh well currently it is  in  some sort of trouble i i cannot really  delve into it right now another world  that is under your protection is a  forged wolf that is actually uh under  mechanicus rule but uh  it is within your trade empire so you  have some relationship with it you will  have your capital where you will  interact with some  noble houses that were given titles uh  by different members of your dynasty but  for example i mentioned the forge world  within your within your empire it is up  to you to choose what will be produced  there and  some of the things that you can decide  to produce here  are not as legal  or  as  loyal to the imperium several things  that we consider to be serpg  cornerstones one of them are companions  when we mention crpg we always  mean it to be companion focused so we  will have companions and those companies  will not be just  units that travel with you and  they will have their stories they will  have their dialogues they will interrupt  your uh dialogues and add things that  they think they can disagree with you  and sometimes these disagreements can  become violent and they can also  disagree with each other there are  tensions between some factions are quite  high so as you might imagine for example  adapter serratus or  space marine can  be quite  wary of zenith in your party another  thing that we consider to be inherent  part of what rpg is  is uh basically playing with your role  having your role not being just a thing  you assume during your during your  playthrough but the things that you can  play with so you can define it you can  change it and this means that we want  your choices to really matter to change  who you are how people react to you and  so there will be numerous places within  the game where you can change the way uh  the world will work from now sometimes  in mineral issues sometimes in more  major no other warhammer 40 000 game has  boasted this much choice freedom  exploration or interaction with its  universe but with the extra depth the  crpg allows comes the risk of players  that are new to the franchise feeling  overwhelmed or lost within webs of lore  and buzzwords this has often been an  issue and it's come to me pitching  warhammer 40 000 to my friends that  might be interested but it appears that  owlcat has similar thoughts and are  building this game with both depth and  approachability in mind when it comes to  players exploring the rogue trade as  corona's expanse the imperial presence  there exists but it isn't  as complete as within other sectors so  there are still places to explore still  places to find stuff that wasn't uh  seen by humans warhammer lore while it  is expansive and deep in places is not  open to  normal citizen within the imperium  basically the lower you are in your  station the less you will actually know  this ties greatly into our idea of  explaining it to you because at the  start of the game you're uh just living  in the on the ship basically and from  this on onwards with can we explain to  you first what rogue trader is  what exactly is happening at all there  then we can explain like how imperium  works uh then we can explain what zenas  chaos and so on and delve deeper and  deeper into some things rogue trader  seems to want to allow players to  experience more than the combat and war  of warhammer 40 000. while battles and  bloodshed will still be a core part of  the game as with any other crpg the  genre allows the other parts of life in  the 41st millennium to shine a little  brighter for those stories to be told  and those characters and archetypes to  be fleshed out in a way that may not  have been possible in a game that's set  primarily on a battlefield people who  are not delving deep into warhammer lore  that this is like a setting only about  war where like space marine skill works  and nothing else basically happens it's  always world war and uh and they just  assume that the setting kind of makes no  sense while people who like read black  library books they know that there are  forge worlds where all this stuff has  produced high walls where billions  of people live and where the armies of  imperium are grown and trained it's not  exactly about the lack of war it's more  about there's also other stuff it gets  to explore uh like an uninhabited world  graveyards of civilizations it gets to  explore  how frontier works how planets get into  imperium how it happened that imperium  spans a whole galaxy it's because of  people basically like you these are  pretty lofty goals for warhammer 40000's  first crpg but if our cat can accomplish  them then rogue trader will allow  players to interact and explore the  universe of 40k in a way that we've just  not seen before and hopefully in a way  that will appeal to both the die hard  fans of the collection of black library  books and piles of plastic to those who  are just first entering into the world  of 40k to the people who want the  intense combat and to see a space marine  in action or even to the players out  there who want to see what 40k is life  beyond the barrel of a bulk in the grim  dark future there may only be war  but that doesn't mean that there isn't  anything else  thank you so much for watching i hope  you enjoyed and can tell i'm very  excited about this game if you are as  well let me know your thoughts in the  comment section below or tweet me at a  regular dave make sure to like the video  subscribe for more like this and i'll  see you in the next one  [Music]

